      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "BCR-ABL inhibition made molecularly targeted therapy a decisive clinical reality in chronic myeloid leukemia.",
        "attribution": "Druker, Lydon, and Sawyers capture key therapeutic-development, drug-discovery, and clinical-validation contributions.",
        "maturity": "The benefit is sustained, transformative, and foundational for precision cancer medicine.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discovery-to-treatment chain also depends on important earlier BCR-ABL and disease-biology work not represented in the candidate framing."
